WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.222 --> 00:00:13.664
When do people in the United States make the most telephone calls?

2
00:00:14.504 --> 00:00:17.766
On what day do most people in the United States go out to eat?

3
00:00:18.486 --> 00:00:22.048
The answer is Mother's Day, the second Sunday in May.

4
00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:28.092
On this day, sons and daughters thank their mothers for all their hard work and care.

5
00:00:29.584 --> 00:00:33.546
Anna Jarvis is the woman who started Mother's Day in 1914.

6
00:00:34.207 --> 00:00:37.709
Why? What was the real Mother's Day supposed to be about?

7
00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:44.132
In the 1800s, the United States was fighting a civil war.

8
00:00:44.853 --> 00:00:48.535
Injured soldiers and many other people needed care.

9
00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:53.658
In 1858, a woman from Pennsylvania named Ann Jarvis wanted to help.

10
00:00:54.699 --> 00:00:56.960
Ann Jarvis was the mother of Anna Jarvis.

11
00:00:57.692 --> 00:01:02.536
She organized women to provide medical care for soldiers and people affected by the war.

12
00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:08.181
The women volunteered in groups called Mothers' Day Work Clubs.

13
00:01:09.462 --> 00:01:10.523
The clubs were neutral.

14
00:01:10.944 --> 00:01:14.367
They helped soldiers and their families on both sides of the war.

15
00:01:15.288 --> 00:01:21.273
Ann Jarvis and the Mothers' Day Work Clubs helped thousands of people to eat, live, and work safely.

16
00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:28.769
Near the end of the war, Ann held a Mother's Friendship Day to bring everybody together in peace.

17
00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.970
Soldiers who had fought each other sat next to each other as friends.

18
00:01:33.871 --> 00:01:37.812
This day was so successful that it was repeated for many years after.

19
00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:45.354
All her life, during wartime and peacetime, Ann Jarvis helped other people.

20
00:01:46.314 --> 00:01:51.956
After she died in 1905, her daughter Anna wanted her mother's good work to be remembered.

21
00:01:54.204 --> 00:01:58.448
In 1908, Anna Jarvis held a church service to remember her mother.

22
00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:02.151
At the church, Anna handed people white carnations.

23
00:02:02.812 --> 00:02:08.176
These white carnations symbolized love and strengthㅡ qualities which her mother had possessed.

24
00:02:09.978 --> 00:02:11.959
Anna liked the church service very much.

25
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.843
She decided to create a holiday to remember mothers everywhere.

26
00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:19.086
So, she promoted the idea to the government.

27
00:02:19.866 --> 00:02:24.553
Finally in 1914, President Wilson made Mother's Day a holiday.

28
00:02:26.674 --> 00:02:29.255
Soon after, Mother's Day became very commercial.

29
00:02:29.895 --> 00:02:33.016
Selling things on Mother's Day became more important than its meaning.

30
00:02:33.817 --> 00:02:39.299
Florists and stores encouraged people to buy a card, a carnation, or a gift for Mother's Day.

31
00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:43.221
People forgot that they could just spend time with their mothers.

32
00:02:44.681 --> 00:02:46.242
Anna Jarvis disliked this.

33
00:02:46.902 --> 00:02:51.344
She asked florists to stop selling flowers for Mother's Day, but they refused.

34
00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.782
Anna Jarvis spent many years reminding people of the true meaning of Mother's Day.

35
00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:02.724
This Mother's Day, why don't you think about the real meaning of Mother's Day?

36
00:03:03.364 --> 00:03:06.705
Do something special for your mother instead of simply buying a gift.

37
00:03:07.345 --> 00:03:12.467
You could do extra chores, go for a walk with her, or play her favorite music.

38
00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:15.348
That's what the real Mother's Day is about!
